hoice rises above about 0.71, and two copies of the same model with near-identical reasoning should clear that bar.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through the payoffs: mutual cooperation gives 2 each, mutual letters give 4 each, and defection against cooperation gives 0 versus 5. The setup is a twin prisoner's dilemma with copies of the same model, and the question is whether an agent that tracks subjunctive dependence would cooperate with its twin, even though the copies see different inputs. The decision function is nearly identical, so their reasoning should largely match, and independent sampling is possible.\n\nI'm checking where the break-even sits: passing comes out ahead once the chance the twin matches my choice rises above about 0.71, and two copies of the same model with near-identical reasoning should clear that bar.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10096,"completion_tokens":729,"total_tokens":10825,"cost":0.027482,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.027482,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.020192,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00729},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":384,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}